I even  themed my whole room around Pokemon but  what was really important is that it  opened the door to something new for me  Digimon cardcaptors Dragon Ball Z all  these unique animations that were unlike  any other cartoons that were available  and while I didn't know the exact name  of what they were I was discovering a  new world I wanted to see more of I  didn't know it but this was the start of  my anime fandom I was 12 years old when  I got my first wake-up call my pencil  case that was filled with pokemon theme  stationery was dropped and the entire  content was spilled out in full view in  front of a group of girls and it wasn't  just any girls it was the popular girls  they looked at it they led to me and  burst out laughing telling me I'd never  get a girlfriend in my life if I haven't  grown our Pokemon yet to this day I have  never felt so much shame for enjoying  something I love and from then on until  just as I was reaching for adulthood I  never told a single soul that I liked  anime thinking back the ironic thing is  I was still a kid liking things that  kids should like unfortunately though  that's the way things were and as I grew  older I started to properly learn what  anime actually was and my love for it  only increased every week I was  discovering new shows better than the  last new universes to explore characters  to know stories to get absorbed in and I  had to keep it all to myself which at  the time was pretty easy I was that  quiet kid in class that no one really  noticed or cared for I didn't have a  group or clique I wasn't part of any  after-school clubs or anything school  passed me by and that was it I had  nowhere to belong there maybe I never  did but to me that was fine because what  I alone knew was that when the bell rang  and I could go home there was a whole  nother world that I could be a part of a  fantastical world where you can be  anything ninjas pirates samurai fighting  against the greater odds mecha pilots  taking part in the most advanced Wars  you can imagine or being at the center  of a harem where girls are actually  interested in someone like you of course  it was in the real world I knew it was  in the real world but the beauty of it  was for a moment for that brief period  it allowed me to just forget it sounds  stupid now but some of the highlights of  my adolescence was discovering my love  for anime it was a time that I could  easily get away from the world for just  a bit  my way to take five from life and I  think this is a reason I found it so  hard to get into slice-of-life anime I  can wrap my head around why you'd want  to watch a reflection of something I  wanted to escape on I just couldn't  relate as I reach the end of my  adolescence after years of conditioning  telling me that I would grow out of this  phase eventually I wondered why I hadn't  I wondered if it was normal seeing as I  was the a person I knew who was so into  this stuff still maybe I was just weird  maybe I'd be living with my mum for the  rest of my life or maybe I would grow of  this eventually right what I did fully  understand back then and what I wish I  did was that I wasn't alone and I know  I'm not the only one who thought this  see there were group of us who had the  same routine doppelgangers rushing back  to school to catch the latest episode of  Dragon Ball Z on Toonami mischievously  staying up late to watch the elusive  cowboy bebop on Adult Swim or pretending  to throw your tiara like you're part of  Sailor Moon if you're a go of course the  boys would just secretly mine me the  Kamehameha way whenever they could we  all thought we were by ourselves we all  thought we were the only ones but what  we didn't realize was that these TV  networks were speaking to a whole  generation a generation we didn't even  know we were a part of until the  Internet gave us a voice a whole  community and a place together suddenly  we saw there were others everywhere just  like us hiding there all along not only  in anime but every facet of nerd culture  gaming comics cartoons it didn't matter  we all wanted to be heard and boy did  the world listen being a nerd suddenly  wasn't looked down on anymore in fact it  was cool gaming started to be accepted  by everyone comic book movies made  liking superheroes a cool thing and  people actually started to learn what  the hell anime was not only that but we  had more of it than ever before nerd  stuff wasn't just being made by some old  farts anymore nerd stuff was being made  by other nerds inspired by everything  that came before them and who truly  understand the audience they were  appealing to because they were one of us  instead of people growing out of it  you have people growing back into it  even the jocks you knew nothing about to  school now have something small in  common with you the whole culture is  changed in the time I've grown up and  what  and people ask me why I want animates  become more popular maybe I'll come up  with some argument about how more fans  would help the industry create more  awesome stuff which is not untrue but  deep inside I don't ever want anyone to  be made to feel ashamed for being  absolutely passionate about this medium  like I was  we are graduates from a class of only  90s kids will remember only 80s kids  were relate only 70s kids were truly  appreciate a generation that had the  force with them going back to the future  who wanted to be the best like no one  ever was so will we grow out of it like  we were told when we were kids well we  will grow order grow wiser or dumber  maybe and change over time which is  inevitable it's easy to look forward in  the future and think that you are the  person you are and nothing will ever  change that  yet look back in the past and realize  how much you've changed and learned  every year no matter who you are in the  world living an adult life is different  from your adolescence perhaps your  interest will change perhaps your  burnout and have less time to spend on  the hobby and perhaps other commitments  will take over who knows but I don't  think there will ever be a point when  you'll get bored of feeling that same  excitement you did as a kid experiencing  or discovering something truly wonderful  maybe it was geeking out when you saw  the Avengers Assemble for the first time  in live action getting shocked when  watching Madoka Magica for the first  time or dropping in all in some of one  punch man's fights that feeling will be  something we can never grow out of even  if it doesn't come as easily as we grow  older you'll grow out of anime they said  you'll grow out of gaming they said  you'll grow out of comics they said  except we didn't we never grew out of it  we're growing up with it  you
 

